+  THE INTERNAL EVIDENCE, re-verified against PROD on 2026-08-11 by this task rather than taken
+  from the issue text: Mação (4767) is a participant in **0** fixtures warehouse-wide and its
+  only events anywhere are these 10; Macau (1544) is a participant in exactly the 2 fixtures
+  whose events are mis-tagged. 4767 exists in `dim_team` only as an attribution artefact.
+
+  WHY `reattribute_if_cohabiting` AND NOT `alias`, since the two modes are not interchangeable
+  and the wrong one fails in opposite directions. `alias` is an UNCONDITIONAL id replacement and
+  means "one club, two provider ids" — it would permanently conflate a Portuguese municipality
+  with a national team, so if Mação ever legitimately appeared in Portuguese football its events
+  would be silently folded into Macau. `reattribute_if_cohabiting` fires only where the correct
+  id IS a fixture participant and the wrong id is NOT, which is exactly the ASKO Kara precedent
+  already in this seed (#526). The failure modes are asymmetric: `alias` is silently wrong
+  forever, `reattribute_if_cohabiting` is at worst inert.
